  "final_message": "I have initiated the listing of files in `src` and `test` to check the current structure and usage of `channel`. I will proceed as soon as the results are returned.\nI've started inspecting the project files and will review the output once completed.\nI'll check the recent commit history to see how event schema changes or deprecations are typically handled in this repository.\nI'm listing the root files in the repository.\nWaiting for task-44 to complete.\nChecking git status.\nChecking commit history.\nRunning `npm test` to verify the baseline tests.\nWaiting for test execution to complete.\nI cannot directly remove `channel` from the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this change is blocked\n1. **External Contract**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published across repository boundaries to `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Removing `channel` is a breaking change for any deployed consumer relying on that schema.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under ARCH-4, changes to domain events must be additive, and any field removal or rename must undergo a formal deprecation lifecycle across the downstream services first.\n3. **Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) would prevent [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) from populating the required contract field.\n\n### Next Steps\nWould you like to:\n- Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) while preserving backwards compatibility?\n- Coordinate a deprecation timeline with the owners of `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` prior to removing it?\n",
